-- title:
--   Crossing exponent at supersingular nodes, all characteristics q∤ N
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a level $N\neq 0$, an algebraically closed field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring map $\mathrm{red}:A\to k$; fix modular polynomial data $\Phi$ for $q$ (monic in $\mathbb Z[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(q)$, vanishing on the pair $(j,j_q)$) together with the Kronecker congruence $\Phi \bmod q=(X^q-Y)(X-Y^q)$, integrality of the two degeneracy maps from level $N$ to level $Nq$, a place specialisation $P$ of the level-$N$ situation at $A$ over $k$, and a prolongation tuple $R$ over $P$. Assume $q\nmid N$, that $R$ is a model (the two divisor laws and the two cusp laws at the infinity and zero sides), that $W$ is a finite set of places of the geometric level-$N$ function field over $k$ all of which are supersingular (rational, affine for $j$ and $j_N$, with supersingular $j$-value), that $R$ satisfies the regularity law and the node-value law for $W$ and the order law at places fixed by the square of the geometric Frobenius, and that $\ker(\mathrm{red})$ is the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $K\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$ be a number field and put $\mathcal O=A\cap K$, with reduction $\mathrm{red}$ restricted to $\mathcal O$. Let $w\in W$, let $x_w\in\mathcal O$ reduce to the $j$-value $w(j)$, let $\varpi\in\mathcal O$ generate the kernel of the reduction on $\mathcal O$, and write $q=\varpi^{e_K}\varepsilon$ with $\varepsilon$ a unit of $\mathcal O$. Let $c$ be a node-coordinate datum at $w$ over $K$, i.e.\ elements $x,y$ of the ring of functions of the level-$Nq$ field over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ that are integral for both prolongations, integral at every place reducing to $w$ along the first degeneracy, and with expansion in the subfield generated by the constants from $\mathcal O$ together with $j$ and $j_{Nq}$, such that $x$ reduces to $0$ under the first residue and has order $1$ at the Frobenius-translate of $w$ under the second, while $y$ reduces to $0$ under the second residue and has order $1$ at $w$ under the first. If $x\,y=\nu_w(\varpi)^{E}u$ with $u$ a unit of that ring and $\nu_w$ the map sending a constant of $\mathcal O$ into it, then $E=\mathrm{placeWidthChar}_q(N,w)\cdot e_K$, where $\mathrm{placeWidthChar}$ is the characteristic-$q$ width $12$ or $1$ at $j=0$ or $j\neq0$ for $q=2$, $6$ or $1$ at $j=0$ or $j\neq0$ for $q=3$, and $\mathrm{jWidth}(j)$ otherwise, divided by the ramification index of $w$ over the $j$-line.
--
--   This is the local crossing equation $xy=\varpi^{\,\text{width}\cdot e_K}$ of the special fibre of the level-$Nq$ modular curve at a supersingular node, in the form needed for the two components of the fibre at $q\nmid N$. Unlike the companion result, which assumes $5\le q$, no lower bound on $q$ is imposed here, so the wild widths $12$ (for $q=2$, $j=0$) and $6$ (for $q=3$, $j=0$) are included; it feeds the chart-width comparison and the construction of inertia-fixed node presentations.
